# Class Rules (topic creation)

## Product
- One lesson = self-contained `classes/NN/index.html` (CSS + JS inline). No build step.
- Target: Slovak grades 8–9, online 1× ~45–60 min. CEFR aim per course: solid **A2 → emerging B1** grammar core (not “all English grammar”).
- Follow Martin worksheet spine: Grammar Review → Listening (4 blocks) → T/F → Scrambled Dialogue → New Topic → Grammar Box → Classroom/Grammar matching.

## Before writing content
Ask only if missing: (1) class number, (2) topic, (3) unit transition, (4) main grammar focus from `curriculum/25-hours.md`.

## Content rules
- Listening: 4 paragraphs, ~80–100 words each; 5 gaps + scrambled 5-word bank per block; full text word-for-word synced with gap text.
- T/F: 8–10 items, factual to listening only.
- Dialogue: 6 Jim questions + Pete scrambled answers; accept flexible order via `DIALOGUE_KEY`.
- Grammar Review must match the hour’s focus and recycle 1–2 prior hours.
- Optional **Sentence Transformations** pool: per tense 3 lemmas × 3 forms (affirmative/negative/question = 9 sentences); random New set; Check with flexible answers (`don't`/`do not`).
- Section 7: 11 English terms → 3 Slovak options each; Unicode `\u` in JS hints.
- Slovak diacritics: prefer `\uXXXX` in JS strings to avoid mojibake.

## UX / app rules
- Desktop web layout (not A4): `.wrap` up to ~1480px; listening / dialogue / matching in 2 columns on wide screens; collapse under 1100px; A4 only in `@media print`.
- Sticky toolbar: first control is `← Home` linking to `../../`; then Show Full Text, Copy controls, Clear Answers.
- Check Dialogue / Check Score: sticky bar **inside** Section 4 / 7 (not only global toolbar); no `scrollIntoView` jump.
- Show/Hide toggles; hide check feedback on focus/edit.
- `localStorage` key unique per class: `esl-class-NN-v1`.
- Update root `index.html` hub link when adding a class.

## Honesty constraint
Do not promise “full English grammar in 25 hours”. Promise a **recycled functional core** (see curriculum). Each new topic carries old grammar forward.
